%description:
ErrorModelBase: a missing bit error rate of any error model

The same check for an error model that returns a packet error rate of 1 and a NaN bit error rate (corruptionMode = "chunk"): the message names the class of the error model and the corruption mode, not a parameter of some other error model.

Two ad-hoc IEEE 802.11 hosts, 20 m apart, multicast frames.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "inet.test.moduletest.lib.ConstantRatesErrorModel"
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.packetErrorRate = 1
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.corruptionMode = "chunk"
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-80211.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep -h '<!>' test.out test.err > errors.out || true
%contains: errors.out
Error model inet::ConstantRatesErrorModel cannot provide a bit error rate for corruptionMode = "chunk"; use corruptionMode = "packet" or an error model that computes a bit error rate
